
SIREN number :
Système d'Identification du Répertoire des ENtreprises
is 9 digits long
this number define the legal entity of the company, there is always only one legal entity


SIRET number :
Système d'Identification du Répertoire des ÉTablissements
is 14 digits long
this number define one of the physical incarnation of the legal entity, like one wearhouse, or one selling point
this number is unique per phisical entity
the SIRET is defined as SIREN + NIC (Numéro Interne de Classement) 5 digits

NIC number :
is 5 digits long
is used as a compliment to the SIREN to make the SIRET
first 4 digits is the comune (location) code, the last one is a incrementing number for the count of entitys
on NIC[4] overflow they use leters so it give total of 36 positions


NAF code :
Nomenclature d'Activités Française
is 5 symbols long
is a map of code to value of french profecional accivities
the codes are always [0-9][0-9].[0-9][0-9][A-Z]
the NAF[0-1] define the main category
the NAF[2-3] define the case in a category, the category is like the class and the case is the specialization

APE code :
Activité Principale Exercée
same as NAF



trancheEffectifsEtablissement :
